d_62f30f01b57e4'),(67315,1848,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(67316,1848,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(67317,1848,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(67318,1848,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(67319,1848,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(67320,1848,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(67321,1848,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(67322,1848,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(67323,1848,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(67324,1848,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(67325,1848,'problem_icons','4'),(67326,1848,'_problem_icons','field_640fa0191d518'),(67327,1848,'ceh_content_left',''),(67328,1848,'_ceh_content_left','field_640e97e8f1c8c'),(67329,1848,'ceh_content_right',''),(67330,1848,'_ceh_content_right','field_640e97fdf1c8d'),(67331,1848,'pc_content_left',''),(67332,1848,'_pc_content_left','field_640e983bf1c8f'),(67333,1848,'pc_content_right',''),(67334,1848,'_pc_content_right','field_640e984df1c90'),(67335,1848,'problem_icons_1_prob_icon','