1970,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(102030,1970,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(102031,1970,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(102032,1970,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(102033,1970,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(102034,1970,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(102035,1970,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(102036,1970,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(102037,1970,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(102038,1970,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(102039,1970,'problem_icons','4'),(102040,1970,'_problem_icons','field_640fa0191d518'),(102041,1970,'ceh_content_left',''),(102042,1970,'_ceh_content_left','field_640e97e8f1c8c'),(102043,1970,'ceh_content_right',''),(102044,1970,'_ceh_content_right','field_640e97fdf1c8d'),(102045,1970,'pc_content_left',''),(102046,1970,'_pc_content_left','field_640e983bf1c8f'),(102047,1970,'pc_content_right',''),(102048,1970,'_pc_content_right','field_640e984df1c90'),(102049,1970,'problem_icons_1_prob_icon','1699'