,2006,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(104905,2006,'report_link_text','Download'),(104906,2006,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(104907,2006,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(104908,2006,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(104909,2006,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(104910,2006,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(104911,2006,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(104912,2006,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(104913,2006,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(104914,2006,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(104915,2006,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(104916,2006,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(104917,2006,'problem_icons','4'),(104918,2006,'_problem_icons','field_640fa0191d518'),(104919,2006,'ceh_content_left',''),(104920,2006,'_ceh_content_left','field_640e97e8f1c8c'),(104921,2006,'ceh_content_right',''),(104922,2006,'_ceh_content_right','field_640e97fdf1c8d'),(104923,2006,'pc_content_left',''),(104924,2006,'_pc_content_left','field