515,2071,'_survey_index','field_6294561242236'),(113516,2071,'report_title','Download the report'),(113517,2071,'_report_title','field_62f30edfb57e1'),(113518,2071,'report_intro','Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Phasellus massa erat, consectetur at semper at, feugiat vel orci. '),(113519,2071,'_report_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(113520,2071,'report_link_url','#'),(113521,2071,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(113522,2071,'report_link_text','Download'),(113523,2071,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(113524,2071,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(113525,2071,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(113526,2071,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(113527,2071,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(113528,2071,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(113529,2071,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(113530,2071,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(113531,2071,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(113532,2071,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(113533,2071,'_p