ad the report'),(126057,2201,'_report_title','field_62f30edfb57e1'),(126058,2201,'report_intro','Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Phasellus massa erat, consectetur at semper at, feugiat vel orci. '),(126059,2201,'_report_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(126060,2201,'report_link_url','#'),(126061,2201,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(126062,2201,'report_link_text','Download'),(126063,2201,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(126064,2201,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(126065,2201,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(126066,2201,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(126067,2201,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(126068,2201,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(126069,2201,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(126070,2201,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(126071,2201,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(126072,2201,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(126073,2201,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(126074,2201,'problem_icons'